{
    "background_story": "Collins was the stern but fair gatekeeper of the prestigious Ravenswood Manor. For over two decades, he stood watch at the grand entrance, ensuring that only authorized guests passed through the iron gates. Collins took his job very seriously, knowing that the manor's secrets and inhabitants were his responsibility to protect. He was a master of discretion, able to distinguish between genuine visitors and would-be intruders. Despite his intimidating demeanor, Collins had a soft spot for the manor's children, often sneaking them sweets and stories when their parents were away. As the years went by, Collins became an institution at Ravenswood, respected by all who knew him. His dedication to his post earned him the nickname 'The Guardian of the Gate,' and he remained vigilant, ever ready to defend the manor and its inhabitants.",
